WEBVTT

00:00.950 --> 00:04.530
<i>The more time you spend with someone, 
the more you invariably learn about them.</i>

00:06.870 --> 00:09.640
<i>Her soul is in the early teens at most.</i>

00:10.240 --> 00:14.990
<i>Most of her knowledge's from the internet,
with very little first-hand experience.</i>

00:15.380 --> 00:17.580
<i>She's usually stupidly 
bright and cheerful,</i>

00:19.490 --> 00:20.250
<i>but at times,</i>

00:20.890 --> 00:23.340
<i>she has a look of total resignation 
on her face.</i>

00:24.730 --> 00:27.980
<i>Perhaps her previous life wasn't one 
she could look back fondly upon.</i>

00:28.590 --> 00:29.430
<i>Still...</i>

00:29.430 --> 00:32.180
Aqua, Ruby, dinner's ready.

00:32.710 --> 00:33.820
Coming!

00:36.010 --> 00:38.270
<i>Now that we've been reincarnated,</i>

00:38.840 --> 00:42.410
<i>as long as we're both living our best 
lives now, none of that matters.</i>

00:44.020 --> 00:47.360
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

00:44.020 --> 00:47.360
<b>OSHI NO KO</b>

00:44.020 --> 00:47.360
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

02:14.430 --> 02:16.870
The curry here is great!

02:17.240 --> 02:21.480
Check this out! The marrow-less bones 
can be used as straws!

02:22.500 --> 02:24.870
You can even drink your lassi with them!

02:28.030 --> 02:28.910
Wow!

02:28.910 --> 02:30.420
It's true! This is great!

02:30.420 --> 02:31.050
Right?

02:31.690 --> 02:33.420
Where should we go next?

02:33.420 --> 02:35.820
Everyone here is expecting to drink.

02:35.820 --> 02:40.150
Hmm, places nearby 
where we could drink in peace?

02:40.150 --> 02:40.890
How about Pater?

02:41.210 --> 02:43.580
Oh, I like it.

02:43.580 --> 02:47.750
A friend of mine runs that bar. 
I'll shoot them a LINE message.

02:48.930 --> 02:49.820
<b>Aqua Hoshino</b>

02:50.220 --> 02:51.950
Excuse me a second.

02:51.950 --> 02:53.240
Hey. What's up?

02:53.560 --> 02:54.990
Where are you?

02:54.990 --> 02:58.210
You haven't checked 
any of the items due today.

02:58.210 --> 03:01.740
<i>Uh, I'm out drinking 
with the marketing rep.</i>

03:02.020 --> 03:03.200
Marketing rep?

03:03.740 --> 03:08.860
<i>So they brought a bunch of "friends" 
who are models and actresses,</i>

03:08.860 --> 03:11.360
<i>and you're drinking at a hideaway bar?</i>

03:14.550 --> 03:18.300
I mean, networking is part of their job.

03:19.190 --> 03:22.160
And we always need good actors.

03:22.160 --> 03:23.270
<i>I'm not against it,</i>

03:24.030 --> 03:27.770
<i>but these things tend to be 
full of tough customers.</i>

03:28.240 --> 03:29.360
Don't get eaten alive.

03:33.200 --> 03:37.740
Of course. How many years do you 
think I've spent in this business?

03:43.770 --> 03:48.110
There's a lot about work that 
comes down to human feeling.

03:48.770 --> 03:51.670
Some things you can only see 
with alcohol in your system, too.

03:52.710 --> 03:57.930
This world runs on communication, 
and I'm a pro here.

03:59.840 --> 04:03.140
And pros never lose themselves in booze.

04:03.140 --> 04:06.390
Huh? My phone's gone!

04:06.390 --> 04:07.850
Where'd it go?

04:08.290 --> 04:11.920
Your phone's right here, Director Gotanda.

04:13.200 --> 04:13.900
Aqua-kun.

04:14.360 --> 04:15.710
Could you drag that thing home?

04:15.710 --> 04:17.910
Sure. I'll make sure the skunk gets home.

04:17.910 --> 04:19.110
Oh, hey, kid.

04:19.390 --> 04:21.430
Are you Aqua Hoshino-kun?

04:21.430 --> 04:25.230
I've heard all about you. 
You're the director's best student?

04:24.810 --> 04:26.280
Woohoo!

04:25.230 --> 04:27.570
No. I don't know this man.

04:27.980 --> 04:31.180
Now, now. It's raining 
outside, so join us.

04:31.180 --> 04:32.580
We'll call a taxi for you right away.

04:33.030 --> 04:34.590
Are you hungry?

04:34.590 --> 04:39.460
The Napolitan here is amazing. 
Eat that before you go, at least.

04:39.460 --> 04:40.840
No, thank you.

04:40.840 --> 04:43.020
You're always pestering the young ones.

04:43.020 --> 04:44.680
Give it a rest, Tendouji-san.

04:46.180 --> 04:48.840
Don't go giving me a bad name, now.

04:51.120 --> 04:53.860
Tendouji... Marina Tendouji?

04:53.860 --> 04:55.480
Why, yes.

05:03.470 --> 05:06.470
Did I give you my name?

05:07.580 --> 05:09.620
Here you are. Club soda.

05:09.620 --> 05:13.330
Let's go drinking as soon 
as you're old enough.

05:13.330 --> 05:17.230
But I guess you wouldn't want 
to go with an old lady like me.

05:17.230 --> 05:21.640
Don't worry. I'll bring 
some cute friends with me.

05:24.400 --> 05:26.010
You must love drinking.

05:26.340 --> 05:30.000
It's part of my job, in a way.

05:30.000 --> 05:31.530
Is that really okay?

05:33.320 --> 05:36.140
Doesn't your family worry?

05:36.140 --> 05:39.170
Hey, I'm in my mid-fifties.

05:39.170 --> 05:44.710
And I've been doing this forever, 
so none of them worry about me.

05:46.660 --> 05:47.530
<b></b>May I get to go to a B-Komachi concert

05:47.530 --> 05:48.540
<b></b>May I get permission to go outside

05:48.540 --> 05:53.540
<b></b>May Mom and Dad stay healthy
and never get sick

05:54.170 --> 05:56.040
You know somebody out there does.

05:56.600 --> 05:58.300
I suppose.

05:58.300 --> 06:00.380
I'm married.

06:00.700 --> 06:03.210
See, this is my family!

06:06.470 --> 06:09.520
<i>How is this even possible?</i>

06:11.100 --> 06:14.210
<i>Are there really parents like her?</i>

06:20.160 --> 06:23.450
<i>Sarina-chan...</i>

06:23.450 --> 06:28.910
<b>Happy 54th, Mom!
Don't drink too much</b>

06:24.350 --> 06:26.650
<i>Your life must've been a living hell.</i>

06:27.390 --> 06:28.910
When you have kids,

06:29.210 --> 06:32.620
all that matters 
is that they stay healthy.

06:33.500 --> 06:36.580
Mom... That's why Mom won't come...

06:36.580 --> 06:37.650
No.

06:37.650 --> 06:39.800
You're stuck on this bit again.

06:40.420 --> 06:42.230
Listen, in this scene,

06:42.230 --> 06:46.010
you're a child who starts to understand 
her mother who ran away from her.

06:46.350 --> 06:50.970
You admit that you're abnormal, 
and that your mother doesn't love you.

06:51.750 --> 06:56.780
You let her go, and you set yourself 
free in the process, too.

06:57.170 --> 07:01.120
You need to look relieved, not desperate.

07:00.360 --> 07:01.860
But that's all wrong.

07:03.560 --> 07:08.370
Admitting your mother doesn't love you? 
That can't be right.

07:09.110 --> 07:11.500
It's probably just a misunderstanding.

07:12.370 --> 07:16.370
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

07:12.820 --> 07:15.880
This makes no sense to me.

07:17.310 --> 07:19.130
I mean, after all...

07:19.980 --> 07:22.200
Deep down,

07:22.910 --> 07:25.520
parents always love their kids.

07:28.530 --> 07:29.390
<i>Ibaraki.</i>

07:29.870 --> 07:33.810
<i>Perform at a joint concert 
on an outdoor stage starting 6 PM.</i>

07:34.170 --> 07:35.710
<i>Get in the car at 9 PM.</i>

07:36.350 --> 07:38.100
<i>Back home at 11 PM.</i>

07:38.440 --> 07:40.120
<i>Go to school at 8:30 AM.</i>

07:40.590 --> 07:42.080
<i>Leave early at 10:30 AM.</i>

07:42.570 --> 07:48.530
<b>Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!</b>

07:42.570 --> 07:48.530
<b>Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!</b>

07:42.570 --> 07:47.520
<b>Esperanto Lesson</b>

07:42.570 --> 07:45.660
<i></i>Dig Deep! Chase the Impawsible!<i> 
prep meeting at 11:30 AM.</i>

07:46.220 --> 07:48.530
<i>Film a report at 12 PM.</i>

07:49.110 --> 07:51.650
<i>Get in the car at 3 PM, have lunch,</i>

07:51.650 --> 07:55.620
<i>approve interview text, 
and study for finals.</i>

07:55.620 --> 07:57.330
<b>Yamada        Tanaka        Hoshino        Sasaki        Inoue</b>

07:56.350 --> 07:57.330
<i>And at 4 PM,</i>

07:57.670 --> 08:01.650
<i>attend taping for a late-night 
variety show. Film three episodes.</i>

08:02.890 --> 08:05.880
<i>Practice choreo for a new song at 9:30 PM.</i>

08:06.430 --> 08:09.090
<i>And at the same time, 
discuss YouTube video ideas.</i>

08:09.780 --> 08:12.490
<i>One-on-one acting lessons at 11 PM.</i>

08:13.590 --> 08:16.050
<i>Go to bed at 3 AM.</i>

08:28.430 --> 08:32.620
Mom did all this without breaking a sweat.

08:33.220 --> 08:34.570
I need to do better.

08:35.330 --> 08:39.290
It's okay. I know I can do this.

08:42.380 --> 08:44.490
There's very little time 
before we start filming.

08:45.010 --> 08:49.260
I'd like you to pack Ruby-san's 
schedule with acting lessons.

08:49.610 --> 08:52.090
Ruby's doing all she can.

08:52.090 --> 08:56.200
Her schedule's already packed. 
She barely gets enough sleep.

08:56.200 --> 08:57.180
Even yesterday...

08:57.520 --> 09:00.300
Reduce the amount of work she takes on.

09:00.300 --> 09:02.850
Especially for the duration 
of filming and rehearsals.

09:03.650 --> 09:07.710
<i>The 15-Year Lie</i> will be 
a real test of acting chops.

09:07.710 --> 09:12.200
It might be cruel to say this about 
an actor as inexperienced as Ruby-san,

09:12.610 --> 09:16.360
but even I can see that 
she's lacking in ability.

09:18.700 --> 09:22.560
<i>Where does he get off saying that when he 
produced that </i>Sweet Today<i> live-action?</i>

09:24.190 --> 09:26.880
<i>But he's not wrong.</i>

09:27.260 --> 09:31.560
<i>Ruby doesn't have the skill 
to lead a cast that good.</i>

09:34.340 --> 09:36.050
Hoist the sails, mateys!

09:36.380 --> 09:38.810
Onward ho! To a brand new world!

09:41.800 --> 09:43.230
Not so fast!

09:43.600 --> 09:47.690
Only one of us can get her hands on 
that singular, legendary treasure!

09:47.690 --> 09:50.370
And I'll make sure it won't be you!

09:50.370 --> 09:52.290
Hah! Try me!

09:56.280 --> 09:57.240
<i>It's so hot!</i>

09:57.240 --> 09:58.200
<i>It's so hot!</i>

10:01.460 --> 10:04.710
When summer blazes hot, 
make sweat walk the plank...

10:04.660 --> 10:09.420
<b>Body Wipes</b>

10:04.660 --> 10:09.420
<b>Soap Scented</b>

10:04.660 --> 10:09.420
<b>Spectaclean Body Wipes</b>

10:04.660 --> 10:09.420
<b>Smooth skin
in a jiffy!</b>

10:04.710 --> 10:06.710
...with Spectaclean Body Wipes!

10:06.710 --> 10:09.420
Cut! That's perfect!

10:09.690 --> 10:11.630
Keep going!

10:11.970 --> 10:18.140
I offered you the ad 'cause a big sponsor 
has a <i>Tokyo Blade</i> fan for a daughter,

10:18.140 --> 10:19.600
and you two did great!

10:19.600 --> 10:21.380
I'm honored!

10:19.600 --> 10:21.380
I'm honored!

10:21.380 --> 10:24.690
Wow, you're in perfect sync. 
Your bad blood's all kayfabe, then?

10:26.570 --> 10:30.030
Haha! Of course it is!

10:26.570 --> 10:30.030
Haha! Of course it is!

10:30.030 --> 10:32.700
A rival? Who, her?

10:32.700 --> 10:34.780
Not a chance. 
She's nowhere near good enough.

10:34.780 --> 10:38.280
Wha? You got into it too, Kana-chan.

10:38.610 --> 10:40.540
Don't call me that!

10:43.430 --> 10:47.250
So, what'd you think? Did it help?

10:48.040 --> 10:50.650
You two really are amazing.

10:50.650 --> 10:53.220
You showed me how far I still have to go.

10:53.930 --> 10:56.040
How can I act like you?

10:58.110 --> 11:00.680
Know yourself.

11:01.000 --> 11:05.480
You need to have a good grasp 
of who you are on the inside.

11:06.170 --> 11:07.900
Who I am on the inside?

11:08.360 --> 11:13.200
For example, you take 
your likes and dislikes,

11:13.770 --> 11:17.110
and you either exaggerate 
or play them down as needed.

11:17.790 --> 11:18.630
Right.

11:18.930 --> 11:24.160
That way, you can form new rules 
and associations within your emotions.

11:25.180 --> 11:26.750
That's how you establish a character—

11:27.160 --> 11:29.400
the thing you're having 
trouble with right now.

11:29.400 --> 11:34.090
I place more emphasis on the 
character than myself, though.

11:34.090 --> 11:37.530
That much is obvious. 
You're a method actor.

11:40.410 --> 11:43.040
<i>Know myself?</i>

11:44.190 --> 11:46.840
<i>What kind of person </i>am<i> I?</i>

11:48.510 --> 11:50.770
<i>Am I Ruby?</i>

11:52.350 --> 11:55.540
<i>Am I Sarina Tendouji?</i>

11:57.110 --> 11:58.570
<i>Who am I?</i>

11:58.570 --> 12:00.820
<b>Ichigo: Do you never think about meeting your mom?
Ai: Well, my mother hates me.
Ai: So I probably shouldn't. That's what's better for her, too.</b>

12:02.320 --> 12:05.480
Mother doesn't love me.

12:06.690 --> 12:09.620
No. That can't be true.

12:10.190 --> 12:11.410
I mean...

12:17.970 --> 12:18.880
Mother!

12:19.630 --> 12:23.510
You came to see me! 
How long will you be staying?

12:24.170 --> 12:29.230
After I stop by your grandma's place, 
I have to head back to Tokyo.

12:31.170 --> 12:35.190
Oh. You must be busy with work.

12:35.500 --> 12:36.950
I'm sorry.

12:36.950 --> 12:39.610
I need to go speak to your doctor.

12:39.610 --> 12:42.370
Oh, okay...

12:47.680 --> 12:49.540
Hey, Mother?

12:53.810 --> 12:57.920
Do you love me?

12:58.950 --> 13:00.130
<i>I mean...</i>

13:01.840 --> 13:05.060
<i>There's no way those words were a lie.</i>

13:05.700 --> 13:08.270
Of course I love you.

13:15.980 --> 13:17.980
<b>Tendouji</b>

13:18.340 --> 13:21.990
<i>Many times, I found myself standing 
here when I was feeling down.</i>

13:22.690 --> 13:26.950
<i>My home still stood at the address 
I remembered it at.</i>

13:28.440 --> 13:32.170
<i>If I rang the bell, Mother would answer.</i>

13:33.630 --> 13:36.880
<i>So many times, I thought about 
pressing that button and saying...</i>

13:36.880 --> 13:41.340
<b>Tendouji</b>

13:38.390 --> 13:40.960
Mother, it's me.

13:42.610 --> 13:43.480
<i>But no.</i>

13:56.720 --> 14:02.400
Once upon a time, there was 
a perfectly ordinary family.

14:03.200 --> 14:06.620
As much affection as the mother 
showered the daughter with,

14:06.620 --> 14:10.870
she was found to have a serious 
illness when she was four.

14:11.730 --> 14:17.270
After learning her daughter had less than 
a 10% chance of living another 10 years,

14:17.270 --> 14:19.910
the mother treated her 
with love and care for a while,

14:19.910 --> 14:23.220
but in time, it broke her down mentally.

14:24.970 --> 14:31.310
The father separated the two and focused 
on helping the mother recover.

14:32.440 --> 14:36.230
They came from a respected family 
in the countryside,

14:36.230 --> 14:39.840
so they put the daughter in the care of 
the biggest hospital in their hometown.

14:40.990 --> 14:45.270
The parents threw themselves into work 
as if to run from their sorrows,

14:45.270 --> 14:48.020
and soon they would refuse 
to see reality for what it was.

14:49.500 --> 14:53.880
Eventually, they started to avert 
their eyes from their daughter, too.

14:54.780 --> 14:57.350
My mother used to be a figure skater!

14:57.350 --> 15:01.460
She says she'll teach me how 
to skate once I'm discharged!

15:01.940 --> 15:06.930
I want to make the Olympics 
and put a smile on her face!

15:07.790 --> 15:11.640
The daughter's condition 
only grew worse with time.

15:12.300 --> 15:14.940
She battled chronic headaches and nausea,

15:15.570 --> 15:19.540
and she lost her sense of balance, 
which left her unable to walk.

15:21.630 --> 15:25.030
It affected her memory 
and situational awareness, too.

15:26.340 --> 15:30.240
During those days of suffering, 
she found solace in one special girl.

15:32.260 --> 15:36.410
The daughter came to live 
vicariously through her.

15:37.550 --> 15:43.680
As her condition became terminal, 
the mother stopped showing up at all.

15:44.520 --> 15:47.850
She must not have wanted 
to see her daughter in pain.

15:49.050 --> 15:54.160
But the girl continued 
to wait for her mother.

15:56.230 --> 16:01.310
She continued to wait for her mother, 
believing that she still loved her.

16:06.260 --> 16:08.820
Oh, it's just you, Sensei.

16:08.820 --> 16:11.160
Too bad it's just me.

16:13.060 --> 16:15.200
Hmm? That's, uh, B-Komachi?

16:15.830 --> 16:17.430
They released a new single?

16:17.430 --> 16:18.160
Yep!

16:18.880 --> 16:24.220
The young man had a habit of going to see 
patients who didn't get visitors

16:24.220 --> 16:26.280
and making small talk with them.

16:27.190 --> 16:31.720
It's impossible to quantify just 
how much that helped the daughter.

16:32.750 --> 16:36.100
She had found two rays of hope.

16:37.200 --> 16:43.060
Though she would come 
to lose them both in time.

16:38.100 --> 16:43.570
<b>Ai's Fan for All Eternity!!!</b>

16:45.750 --> 16:50.820
Even as she spent most of her 
short life in a small room,

16:51.320 --> 16:52.960
fought through the pain,

16:53.410 --> 16:55.370
<b>B-Komachi</b>

16:53.800 --> 16:55.370
and had her dreams shattered,

16:56.070 --> 17:00.590
she still continued to wait for 
her mother, day after day.

17:01.570 --> 17:03.790
She continued to believe 
that she was loved.

17:04.830 --> 17:06.500
But even on the day it all ended,

17:07.370 --> 17:10.030
in her final hours,

17:10.030 --> 17:13.340
the mother did not appear before her.

17:15.920 --> 17:19.920
As she heard the news in silence 
in their Tokyo home,

17:21.200 --> 17:24.730
what must've gone through 
the mother's mind?

17:26.190 --> 17:29.000
As a mother who ran 
and ran from her daughter,

17:29.410 --> 17:32.910
what exactly did she even mean to her?

17:34.820 --> 17:37.240
Soon after the girl died,

17:37.990 --> 17:40.670
the mother gave birth 
to a son and daughter.

17:43.210 --> 17:45.800
And now, they all live happily ever after.

17:47.880 --> 17:50.000
All's well that ends well.

17:56.650 --> 18:01.520
I've never seen Mother 
smile like that before.

18:02.710 --> 18:06.560
I knew it. I knew it somewhere deep down.

18:07.720 --> 18:10.440
I wanted her to love me.

18:10.950 --> 18:15.030
But she didn't love me!

18:16.080 --> 18:19.520
That's why I saw Mom as a replacement.

18:19.520 --> 18:22.250
I pushed my disgusting wishes onto her.

18:22.890 --> 18:24.960
What the hell am I?!

18:24.960 --> 18:28.420
Everyone in my life ends up suffering!

18:28.910 --> 18:31.170
All I bring is misfortune!

18:31.860 --> 18:35.800
To Mother, Mom, and Sensei...

18:36.580 --> 18:41.800
Tell me, gods. Why did you 
reincarnate a plague like me?

18:43.370 --> 18:46.770
Sensei, have you ever been to, 
like, Shibuya or Harajuku?

18:47.060 --> 18:49.920
Yeah. I did go to college in Tokyo.

18:49.920 --> 18:51.860
That's so cool!

18:52.110 --> 18:54.570
Those places are full of life, right?

18:55.030 --> 18:58.910
Filled with lots of people, 
and even talent scouts.

18:59.510 --> 19:02.740
Ai said she got scouted in Shibuya, too!

19:02.740 --> 19:03.620
Yeah?

19:04.200 --> 19:07.020
I'll show you around the place 
when you're better.

19:07.020 --> 19:07.830
Really?!

19:08.410 --> 19:10.040
You're really cute,

19:10.040 --> 19:12.540
so I'm sure you'll get 
approached by scouts.

19:13.010 --> 19:17.520
But I'll send scouts from underground idol
groups and other shady places packing.

19:17.520 --> 19:21.220
But I'd love to be an idol, 
underground or not.

19:21.620 --> 19:24.020
I want to be like Ai 
and wear stylish outfits,

19:24.020 --> 19:27.650
sing cute songs, 
have the crowds do calls for me,

19:28.020 --> 19:29.730
take the stage in huge venues,

19:29.730 --> 19:32.260
and put smiles on lots of people's faces!

19:33.180 --> 19:34.500
That's so dreamy!

19:34.500 --> 19:36.030
Not a chance.

19:36.560 --> 19:39.140
Show business is a scary place.

19:39.140 --> 19:43.180
I won't allow it unless you have a good 
agency repping and looking out for you.

19:43.180 --> 19:45.370
Jeez, you're too overprotective!

19:54.200 --> 19:56.670
Why did I even become an idol?!

19:58.550 --> 19:59.640
Take it easy.

20:00.040 --> 20:01.690
Take a deep, long breath.

20:02.590 --> 20:05.310
You need to lie down. Can you stand?

20:06.470 --> 20:07.670
The script...

20:08.130 --> 20:09.410
Where's my script?

20:10.470 --> 20:12.160
I need to rehearse.

20:12.160 --> 20:13.730
You're in no state for that.

20:14.230 --> 20:15.640
Come on, grab on to me.

20:15.640 --> 20:17.450
I don't want your help, Aqua!

20:19.470 --> 20:23.240
That's right. The reason I'm an idol

20:24.370 --> 20:29.710
is so I can make it to the top and find 
the guy who killed Mom and Sensei.

20:30.120 --> 20:32.670
To avenge Mom and Sensei!

20:33.200 --> 20:35.720
I'll find him if it's the last thing I do.

20:35.720 --> 20:38.860
And I'll make him regret 
ever coming into this world!

20:40.980 --> 20:42.050
Stop that.

20:42.620 --> 20:47.430
Living for revenge will bring you 
nothing but pain and suffering.

20:47.990 --> 20:50.940
There's no need for you to do that.

20:51.960 --> 20:52.690
Please.

20:53.850 --> 20:56.830
Forget about revenge 
and live your own life.

20:57.530 --> 20:59.400
Don't tell me what to do.

21:00.010 --> 21:02.640
Quit trying to act like my big bro now.

21:02.640 --> 21:06.740
I don't see you as real family.

21:07.370 --> 21:12.640
We're total strangers. We just happened 
to be reborn in the same place.

21:14.590 --> 21:17.460
Fine. You're free to think that.

21:18.820 --> 21:21.920
I'm not about to call us 
brother and sister now.

21:22.410 --> 21:24.680
I know I have no right to.

21:25.430 --> 21:27.640
And I'm fully aware 
that I'm being a hypocrite.

21:28.450 --> 21:29.520
But...

21:29.830 --> 21:32.520
I'm not asking as Aqua Hoshino.

21:32.990 --> 21:34.730
Please listen to <i>me,</i>

21:35.220 --> 21:36.420
Sarina-chan.

21:38.000 --> 21:41.200
I know this isn't why 
you wanted to be an idol.

21:42.180 --> 21:43.910
You got out of that hospital room.

21:44.290 --> 21:46.700
You're finally free to live 
the life you want.

21:47.950 --> 21:50.600
Didn't you want to be like Ai 
and wear stylish outfits,

21:50.600 --> 21:53.980
sing cute songs, 
have the crowds do calls for you,

21:53.980 --> 21:57.120
take the stage in huge venues, 
and put smiles on lots of people's faces?!

21:58.030 --> 22:01.520
Didn't you become an idol 
to make those dreams come true?!

22:02.490 --> 22:07.390
<i>A singular thought, "What if?" 
has crossed my mind time and time again.</i>

22:08.720 --> 22:11.600
<i>Every time I felt I saw 
traces of Sarina-chan in you,</i>

22:11.600 --> 22:13.400
<i>I turned around and beat myself up.</i>

22:14.310 --> 22:18.210
<i>I hated myself for ever having 
such self-serving fantasies.</i>

22:19.560 --> 22:22.500
<i>After being powerless 
to do anything to help Sarina-chan,</i>

22:22.500 --> 22:24.860
<i>there was no way I'd ever 
get a second chance.</i>

22:25.580 --> 22:28.240
<i>But all these years,</i>

22:28.790 --> 22:31.490
<i>I've treated you just like 
I would have treated her.</i>

22:32.430 --> 22:35.080
Forget about revenge.

22:36.140 --> 22:37.970
I'm begging you, Ruby.

22:39.310 --> 22:40.350
Why?

22:41.530 --> 22:43.150
Why are you crying?

22:44.340 --> 22:48.080
Why did you just call me Sarina?

22:49.700 --> 22:53.230
How do you know 
about that time in the hospital?

22:54.670 --> 22:55.690
Tell me...

22:56.780 --> 22:59.240
Could it be...?

23:01.140 --> 23:03.980
Are you Sensei?

23:08.870 --> 23:11.720
I've been looking for this.

23:13.240 --> 23:15.290
You held onto it for me, huh,

23:16.350 --> 23:17.670
Sarina-chan?

24:08.600 --> 24:11.420
Sensei!

24:11.760 --> 24:15.450
You've always been this close?

24:15.450 --> 24:16.390
Why?

24:16.730 --> 24:18.850
Why did you never tell me?

24:19.630 --> 24:23.140
Uh, I wasn't sure until just now.

24:23.140 --> 24:24.730
You dummy!

24:24.730 --> 24:26.930
I worked so hard!

24:26.930 --> 24:32.330
I thought you'd find me if 
I called myself a B-Komachi idol.

24:32.710 --> 24:37.290
I always looked for you 
among the crowd at every event.

24:37.290 --> 24:40.290
I thought you might be 
somewhere out there watching,

24:40.290 --> 24:43.130
so I gave my all each time!

24:43.880 --> 24:47.940
I was worried you'd forgotten 
all about Mom and B-Komachi,

24:48.420 --> 24:51.240
and that maybe you'd never find me.

24:52.390 --> 24:56.780
I called the hospital and 
they said you were missing.

24:56.780 --> 24:58.230
And then what?

24:58.830 --> 25:01.190
I find you dead in a cave?

25:01.560 --> 25:04.270
I'm sorry. I put you through a lot.

25:04.920 --> 25:10.360
I trusted you, Aqua, but then 
you went and sold Mom out.

25:10.910 --> 25:15.660
It made me feel like I couldn't 
trust anybody in the world.

25:15.660 --> 25:17.280
I didn't forget.

25:18.150 --> 25:23.250
I told the world about Ai's secret and 
spurred the director to make this movie

25:24.080 --> 25:26.750
all to get revenge for Ai.

25:28.590 --> 25:32.890
I thought I had to avenge Mom and you,

25:32.890 --> 25:35.890
<b>Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!</b>

25:32.890 --> 25:35.890
<b>Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!</b>

25:32.890 --> 25:35.890
<b>Special Episode Pitch</b>

25:33.680 --> 25:35.890
so I did lots of awful things.

25:36.510 --> 25:38.950
I told lots of lies.

25:39.310 --> 25:42.610
Every time I did, 
a pain shot through my chest,

25:42.610 --> 25:45.520
and I felt a knot in my stomach.

25:46.350 --> 25:52.520
The more I lied, the more I felt I was 
drifting away from what I wanted to be.

25:52.950 --> 25:56.510
Ruby, that stuff is not you.

25:57.520 --> 25:58.410
But...

25:58.820 --> 26:02.110
Mom always said idols 
were made up of lies.

26:02.110 --> 26:04.830
You and Ai are different people.

26:06.750 --> 26:09.090
Stop chasing after her shadow.

26:09.650 --> 26:11.920
Live your own life.

26:12.930 --> 26:14.390
You don't have to lie about anything.

26:16.810 --> 26:19.120
You know, the truth is...

26:19.770 --> 26:21.090
It hurt.

26:21.660 --> 26:27.540
I thought I had to tell believable lies 
and be all smiles all the time like Mom.

26:28.030 --> 26:30.220
I thought I had to be like her.

26:31.590 --> 26:36.180
Being an idol wasn't 
all rainbows and sunshine at all.

26:36.180 --> 26:40.490
So many times, I thought it'd be so much 
easier if I could just forget about her.

26:42.100 --> 26:46.750
When I looked at the fans, sometimes 
I'd think back to her killer's face.

26:46.750 --> 26:53.250
I had all these nasty, 
disgusting thoughts,

26:54.150 --> 26:58.800
but I hid them all because 
I wanted to be loved.

26:59.610 --> 27:04.390
I hadn't changed at all from the time 
I spent hating the world in the hospital.

27:05.570 --> 27:07.690
How can that be good enough?

27:07.690 --> 27:10.190
Am I really good enough like that?

27:11.400 --> 27:14.600
I told you I'd be your 
number one fan, remember?

27:15.550 --> 27:17.070
I said that because,

27:17.690 --> 27:20.530
even as you suffered in pain 
in that hospital room,

27:20.910 --> 27:25.280
you still looked straight ahead with 
stars in your eyes and continued to dream.

27:26.130 --> 27:29.920
Back then, you shone far brighter 
than Ai ever did!

27:34.730 --> 27:36.130
Good for you.

27:36.130 --> 27:38.580
Now Ruby will bounce back,

27:38.580 --> 27:41.970
and you'll get to make your movie 
just like you wanted.

27:42.320 --> 27:46.440
This might just inspire her 
to even greater heights.

27:47.060 --> 27:51.390
If so, that would make me very happy, too.

27:53.310 --> 27:54.030
But...

27:54.690 --> 27:57.520
Are you really sure about this?

27:58.280 --> 28:02.780
It might've been easier for you 
if she'd continued to hate you.

28:08.780 --> 28:10.840
<i>I'll trust you, Onii-chan.</i>

28:11.720 --> 28:16.820
<i>I'll trust that the girl you said you'd be 
a fan of can shine brighter than Mom.</i>

28:18.950 --> 28:20.010
<i>Also...</i>

28:20.340 --> 28:23.010
<i>I haven't forgotten those words.</i>

28:24.310 --> 28:28.960
<i>You said you'd marry me once 
I turned sixteen, remember?</i>

28:31.410 --> 28:36.120
Sensei? I'm sixteen now.

28:39.650 --> 28:41.700
I'm wiped!

28:42.110 --> 28:44.160
Onii-chan, gimme some of your juice.

28:44.440 --> 28:46.260
No. Get your own.

28:47.810 --> 28:51.380
Too late. You snooze, you lose juice.

28:51.730 --> 28:54.130
Ah, I'm coming back to life!

28:54.130 --> 28:55.020
Get off of me.

28:55.020 --> 28:56.290
You're damp with sweat.

28:56.290 --> 28:59.490
Hey, let me have this.

28:59.490 --> 29:01.040
What the hell happened?!

29:01.040 --> 29:04.640
Whoa, you startled me. 
Why'd you start yelling out of nowhere?

29:04.640 --> 29:06.600
We're the ones startled here!

29:06.920 --> 29:08.220
Ever heard of personal space?

29:08.580 --> 29:10.230
You two are stuck together like glue!

29:10.500 --> 29:14.540
Oh, you know how Onii-chan 
and I had been fighting lately?

29:14.540 --> 29:17.190
Well, we made up the other day,

29:18.400 --> 29:20.180
and now we're making up for lost time.

29:20.180 --> 29:21.740
More like <i>over</i>compensating!

29:21.740 --> 29:26.770
You're part of the problem, Aqua! 
Tell your sister off!

29:26.770 --> 29:29.470
I <i>could</i> do that, or I could just 
let her do whatever she wants.

29:29.470 --> 29:31.750
Right. I forgot he was 
obsessed with his sister.

29:31.750 --> 29:33.960
We've always been thick as thieves!

29:35.190 --> 29:36.800
Get off of him already!

29:36.800 --> 29:38.340
Hold it!

29:38.650 --> 29:41.220
They're two hot twins 
that look hot together!

29:41.220 --> 29:43.720
Lemme take pics for Insta!

29:44.930 --> 29:47.640
Ugh, you engagement junkie.

29:50.380 --> 29:52.440
I can't. That was so friggin' weird.

29:52.880 --> 29:55.080
I could smell the degeneracy in the air.

29:56.810 --> 30:00.450
Well, Ruby's got a lot on her plate.

30:00.450 --> 30:04.020
I bet she just wanted somebody to lean on.

30:04.660 --> 30:07.080
She's using him as a crutch, basically.

30:07.920 --> 30:11.540
If it's only as bad as needing an 
emotional support, that's fine.

30:11.540 --> 30:16.300
But the only way to really fix it is to do 
something about her packed schedule.

30:16.750 --> 30:18.710
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

30:16.750 --> 30:20.030
Heck, she's actually 
hit a wall with her acting.

30:20.030 --> 30:22.220
She desperately needs more rehearsal time.

30:22.870 --> 30:25.180
I'm glad she seems to be feeling better,

30:25.180 --> 30:28.380
but motivation and high spirits won't be 
enough to get her through this movie.

30:30.300 --> 30:36.150
If anything, she's at even more risk 
now with this mental doping.

30:36.150 --> 30:39.050
If she goes too hard and breaks down, 
it'll have all been for naught.

30:39.050 --> 30:40.400
Right you are.

30:41.030 --> 30:44.490
But this is Ruby's best chance 
to make a move at superstardom.

30:45.120 --> 30:51.240
Sure, she has to juggle TV appearances, 
events, concerts, and acting lessons...

30:51.240 --> 30:52.690
And her studies, too.

30:52.690 --> 30:53.710
Studies!

30:53.710 --> 30:56.140
Right, those exist!

30:56.140 --> 30:58.920
Mine were so long ago that 
I forgot all about the concept!

30:58.920 --> 31:02.420
I'm amazed you managed to keep up 
your high school girl gimmick like that.

31:02.920 --> 31:05.830
Either way, it'll be hard 
to strike the right balance.

31:05.830 --> 31:09.640
All we can do is hope 
the president takes care of it.

31:10.310 --> 31:13.810
Even if Strawberry Pro 
has experienced this before with Ai,

31:13.810 --> 31:16.600
it was the previous president 
at the helm at the time.

31:17.140 --> 31:21.360
This is probably a real test of 
President Miyako's ability, as well.

31:22.110 --> 31:25.100
Right. We're very grateful.

31:25.100 --> 31:29.650
I'll take a good look at Ruby's 
schedule and get back to you.

31:35.680 --> 31:41.070
Covering a charity event for 
28-Hour TV? That's a huge gig.

31:49.220 --> 31:51.840
<i>I can make room in her schedule.</i>

31:52.250 --> 31:55.850
<i>But do I really want to give 
Ruby even more work?</i>

31:56.730 --> 31:59.020
Reduce the amount of work she takes on.

31:59.840 --> 32:03.560
Especially for the duration 
of filming and rehearsals.

32:06.860 --> 32:09.080
<i>There's so much to think about.</i>

32:13.700 --> 32:18.460
Keep this marketing rep named Tendouji 
as far away from Ruby as possible.

32:19.020 --> 32:20.210
Did something happen?

32:21.160 --> 32:24.410
She's kind of like a relative 
we have history with.

32:25.130 --> 32:27.560
Interacting with her 
could make Ruby unstable.

32:27.990 --> 32:29.660
A relative?

32:30.070 --> 32:34.600
I guess that does happen. 
Tokyo's a small world.

32:35.310 --> 32:39.140
Got it. I'll keep an eye out.

32:39.790 --> 32:40.730
Thanks.

32:46.260 --> 32:49.000
<i>I have to secure time for rehearsals.</i>

32:49.450 --> 32:51.510
<i>But I need to think about her health, too.</i>

32:52.030 --> 32:54.620
<i>And Kana graduates at the end of the year.</i>

32:54.620 --> 32:57.280
<i>How do we replace her in B-Komachi?</i>

32:59.190 --> 33:02.540
<i>As a business owner, 
I should push her as hard as I can.</i>

33:03.270 --> 33:05.980
<i>But what about as her mother?</i>

33:05.540 --> 33:06.630
<b>Congratulations
Entrance Ceremony
Youtou High School</b>

33:08.510 --> 33:11.350
<i>Showbiz is in a constant state of churn.</i>

33:11.350 --> 33:14.090
<i>Most entertainers end up 
as a flash in the pan.</i>

33:14.470 --> 33:19.080
<i>Even if you gain a little fame, it can 
all fade away in just a year's time.</i>

33:19.520 --> 33:26.900
<b>Congratulations
Entrance Ceremony
Youtou High School</b>

33:20.730 --> 33:24.030
<i>There's no doubt that her efforts now</i>

33:24.030 --> 33:26.480
<i>will decide the next ten years 
of Ruby's life and career.</i>

33:27.590 --> 33:32.780
<i>I believe more than anybody else that 
she's capable of reaching the very top.</i>

33:32.780 --> 33:34.510
Listen, Mom!

33:34.510 --> 33:35.490
Yeah?

33:35.490 --> 33:38.450
I'm slowly getting the hang of dancing!

33:37.270 --> 33:38.450
All right!

33:38.450 --> 33:42.250
Soon, we hit the Tokyo Dome! 
The stage of our dreams!

33:39.030 --> 33:40.120
Wow!

33:40.120 --> 33:41.390
Right?

33:41.390 --> 33:43.810
You're a natural!

33:45.480 --> 33:49.270
Ichigo, what would you have done?

33:50.420 --> 33:53.140
<b>Samidare</b>

33:56.260 --> 33:58.800
Barkeep, get me the usual.

33:58.800 --> 34:02.400
Yeah, yeah. The meat'n'veggies set 
with a small rice.

34:02.400 --> 34:04.690
And some mixed veggie juice,

34:04.690 --> 34:06.380
extra kale.

34:06.380 --> 34:08.650
Could you order some 
damn booze for a change?

34:08.950 --> 34:11.090
We're not a diner.

34:12.030 --> 34:16.240
This is the only place I can get 
a proper meal this late at night.

34:17.520 --> 34:22.270
Jeez. Take better care of yourself, 
or you'll die from overwork.

34:22.270 --> 34:26.240
I'd much rather that than let 
one of our talent die from overwork.

34:27.130 --> 34:31.800
Are your kids eating right? 
They're really busy now, yeah?

34:32.090 --> 34:38.710
Mhm. Their manager 
should be taking care of that.

34:38.710 --> 34:40.470
You left it all to someone else?

34:40.980 --> 34:44.490
If you don't look them in the eye 
and keep your arms wide open,

34:44.490 --> 34:46.900
you'll miss the crucial signs.

34:47.470 --> 34:52.700
I get that, but they never 
wear their hearts on their sleeve.

34:53.400 --> 34:58.900
My son's always deadpan, 
my daughter's always all smiles,

34:58.900 --> 35:01.190
and they never complain.

35:02.190 --> 35:05.570
I have no way to tell 
what they're thinking deep down.

35:05.570 --> 35:08.120
I'm not their real mother, after all.

35:12.300 --> 35:16.160
I wanna watch them up close 
all the time too, you know!

35:16.160 --> 35:19.140
I'm not built for all this brainy work!

35:20.100 --> 35:22.980
How I'd love to go back 
to being just a manager if I could!

35:23.940 --> 35:26.940
But this company needs me to do this!

35:27.340 --> 35:29.570
We don't have anybody else to rely on!

35:30.570 --> 35:31.320
Barkeep.

35:31.940 --> 35:33.310
Long time no—

35:35.540 --> 35:37.530
Ichigo...?

35:42.000 --> 35:43.160
Get back here!

35:43.160 --> 35:45.400
I'll be back later!

35:45.790 --> 35:47.290
Yeah, yeah.

35:49.000 --> 35:51.800
Tokyo's a small world, all right.

35:57.720 --> 35:59.890
Hold it, you dolt!

36:07.720 --> 36:09.400
I finally found you.

36:10.040 --> 36:11.770
M-Miyako...

36:12.150 --> 36:13.480
Calm down a se—

36:14.170 --> 36:20.450
Do you have any goddamn idea 
how I've felt all these years?

36:21.550 --> 36:27.680
You abandoned the promise you made me 
to run off and do what, you asshole?!

36:35.340 --> 36:37.300
<b>[Express] Shinjuku Station</b>

36:42.880 --> 36:47.810
<i>The first time I saw Tokyo, it was covered 
in bright lights from top to bottom.</i>

36:48.130 --> 36:51.080
<i>It instantly stole my heart away.</i>

36:54.030 --> 36:58.030
<i>I felt that this city was where 
I was meant to live my life.</i>

36:59.470 --> 37:01.820
<i>The nightlife was like a video game.</i>

37:03.450 --> 37:07.330
<i>I took out the fodder, 
built up XP and gold,</i>

37:07.750 --> 37:09.540
<i>leveled up,</i>

37:09.950 --> 37:12.000
<i>bought more powerful weapons,</i>

37:13.750 --> 37:18.870
<i>spent increasingly more time 
around stupidly loaded people,</i>

37:18.870 --> 37:21.800
<i>started seeing the guys in college 
as snot-nosed brats,</i>

37:22.220 --> 37:29.350
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

37:22.220 --> 37:23.640
<b>A wild Self-Proclaimed Tech CEO appeared!
A wild Self-Proclaimed Investor appeared!</b>

37:22.890 --> 37:27.440
<i>defeated stronger foes, 
built up lots more XP,</i>

37:23.720 --> 37:25.100
<b>Miyako used Blow Kiss!</b>

37:25.140 --> 37:26.390
<b>The Self-Proclaimed Tech CEO was defeated!
The Self-Proclaimed Investor was defeated!</b>

37:26.470 --> 37:27.930
<b>Miyako leveled up!</b>

37:27.440 --> 37:29.350
<i>leveled up even more,</i>

37:28.020 --> 37:29.350
<b>Miyako evolved from
cabaret club girl to lounge girl!</b>

37:29.350 --> 37:32.850
<b>Cabaret Club</b>

37:29.660 --> 37:32.000
<i>switched classes, and grew stronger.</i>

37:30.730 --> 37:32.850
<b>Lounge</b>

37:32.060 --> 37:32.850
<b>Hostess Club</b>

37:33.220 --> 37:36.570
<i>Tokyo's good to strong people like that,</i>

37:36.570 --> 37:39.570
<i>and it affirmed my way of life.</i>

37:40.490 --> 37:45.080
<i>I played the game smart and 
followed this city's unspoken rules,</i>

37:46.400 --> 37:50.800
<i>and I was sure I'd keep 
climbing to ever greater heights.</i>

37:54.670 --> 37:56.380
<b>The hottest, "biggest" new face</b>

37:54.670 --> 37:56.380
<b>Dynamite College Girl!!</b>

37:58.340 --> 38:01.830
<i>But it would all come crashing to an end.</i>

38:03.310 --> 38:05.860
<i>Tokyo was full of attractive girls,</i>

38:05.860 --> 38:10.060
<i>and I didn't have that special 
something to make it in showbiz.</i>

38:11.740 --> 38:16.060
<i>I got more chances to interact with 
big shots due to being an entertainer,</i>

38:16.730 --> 38:18.600
<i>but that didn't last long either.</i>

38:19.190 --> 38:21.650
<b>Checking Inbox</b>

38:19.190 --> 38:20.320
<b>Checking...</b>

38:19.480 --> 38:21.650
<i>By the time I graduated college,</i>

38:20.320 --> 38:21.650
<b>No New Mail</b>

38:21.920 --> 38:25.490
<i>I'd stopped getting invited 
to parties by business owners.</i>

38:26.990 --> 38:29.090
<i>Not that I cared.</i>

38:29.090 --> 38:31.230
<i>Those guys cheated at the drop of a hat.</i>

38:31.230 --> 38:33.710
<i>I would've never found happiness 
in life going out with them.</i>

38:34.630 --> 38:37.340
<i>A Minato-ku trophy girl 
who was no longer in demand</i>

38:37.340 --> 38:42.260
<i>could only stick around by becoming an 
intermediary who summoned younger girls.</i>

38:43.630 --> 38:46.040
<i>And I hung on pathetically 
by doing just that.</i>

38:47.920 --> 38:50.890
<i>More and more men started 
asking me to be their mistress.</i>

38:52.130 --> 38:57.540
<i>Those scumbags are very good at sniffing 
out women at risk of losing their spot,</i>

38:57.540 --> 38:59.900
<i>and they try to exploit them 
for all they're worth.</i>

39:01.060 --> 39:05.700
<i>They use the starry-eyed girls 
until they get tired of them.</i>

39:05.700 --> 39:07.370
Hup.

39:08.610 --> 39:09.390
Heya.

39:18.870 --> 39:23.460
Listen, are you gonna keep 
working the night life forever?

39:34.930 --> 39:38.080
If you don't have a goal in mind, 
wanna come work for me?

39:49.700 --> 39:56.290
<i>I was a girl who longed for the bright 
lights but couldn't cut it in showbiz.</i>

39:54.080 --> 39:56.290
<b>Strawberry Productions</b>

39:56.660 --> 40:01.840
<i>How ironic was it that I'd now be working 
to help others pursue their dreams?</i>

40:03.080 --> 40:03.670
<i>But...</i>

40:04.550 --> 40:08.920
<i>Seeing the lights from backstage 
didn't feel as bad as I'd thought.</i>

40:12.650 --> 40:13.720
Miyako.

40:15.400 --> 40:17.770
Will you stay by my side and support me?

40:18.990 --> 40:20.980
I'll work my butt off.

40:21.840 --> 40:24.090
And if you'll be my pillar—my wife—

40:24.550 --> 40:27.450
I'll show you the most 
dazzling sight in the world.

40:28.330 --> 40:30.800
The most dazzling sight...?

40:32.420 --> 40:34.370
Wow!

40:34.810 --> 40:38.040
I bet it'd feel so good 
if we performed here.

40:38.670 --> 40:42.170
You mean <i>when</i> we perform here.

40:42.170 --> 40:43.160
Right.

40:43.160 --> 40:45.060
It's so huge.

40:45.060 --> 40:46.590
Sure is.

40:46.590 --> 40:48.940
Do you actually think that?

40:48.940 --> 40:50.340
I do, I do.

40:50.340 --> 40:52.230
Really, now?

40:52.230 --> 40:53.800
Really! I mean it!

40:53.800 --> 40:57.810
One day, we'll light up 
Tokyo Dome with glow sticks.

40:58.450 --> 41:00.020
That's our dream.

41:15.660 --> 41:18.210
You said you'd show me!

41:19.820 --> 41:24.250
How could you just throw in the towel 
and run away from it all?!

41:27.630 --> 41:32.300
When I... I still haven't given up on it!

41:36.310 --> 41:40.790
You said it was our dream!

41:51.010 --> 41:55.950
So, Strawberry Productions will undergo 
a major organizational restructuring.

41:56.240 --> 41:58.660
Before that, 
I guess I should introduce you.

42:01.870 --> 42:04.230
That's Ichigo Saitou-kun, 
our new errand boy.

42:04.740 --> 42:06.220
Hello, I'm Saitou.

42:07.710 --> 42:10.860
First, for your new assignments...

42:10.860 --> 42:13.050
Take a look at the handout.

42:13.430 --> 42:15.510
Hayashi will handle 
the cross-media talent.

42:16.010 --> 42:18.600
Streamer Group A goes to Sasami,

42:18.950 --> 42:20.810
and Group B to Terabayashi.

42:21.230 --> 42:24.460
Yoshizumi will manage 
MEM and Arima of B-Komachi.

42:25.030 --> 42:29.280
And I'll take over 
as Ruby and Aqua's manager.

42:30.030 --> 42:31.870
Everything else remains the same.

42:31.870 --> 42:32.820
Huh?

42:32.820 --> 42:36.020
But then, who runs the agency?

42:36.020 --> 42:37.520
Beats me.

42:38.290 --> 42:41.100
Maybe that errand boy over there 
will take care of it.

42:43.470 --> 42:45.110
Who is that?

42:45.110 --> 42:48.270
The president's husband. 
The one who founded this agency.

42:48.270 --> 42:49.050
What?!

42:50.510 --> 42:52.960
That's all from me. Back to work.

42:59.040 --> 43:01.820
Good for you! You got to talk 
things out with Miyako-san!

43:01.820 --> 43:05.020
I can't believe you can say that 
after seeing this face.

43:05.020 --> 43:07.580
I was half coerced into it.

43:07.580 --> 43:09.340
She threatened to sue me,

43:09.340 --> 43:11.650
and when I tried to argue, 
she literally threw hands.

43:12.100 --> 43:14.280
But you came back anyway.

43:14.840 --> 43:17.410
I'm happy for you. 
You wanted to all along, didn't you?

43:22.480 --> 43:26.420
You got me so much work, even 
though you weren't an agent here.

43:26.930 --> 43:30.000
Easier to do that when you're 
officially part of the agency, right?

43:31.550 --> 43:34.760
That's not it. I was set up.

43:36.000 --> 43:37.090
By whom?

43:37.420 --> 43:39.380
Aqua, who else?

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
<b>< Aqua Hoshino</b>

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
We need to talk about Ruby

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
Can you come to Samidare
at 2 AM tonight?

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
Talk about sudden

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
Should a high schooler
really be in the night-life
district that late at night?

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
Won't be a problem

43:39.600 --> 43:42.350
Fine
I might be a little late, though

43:39.600 --> 43:42.310
Thanks

43:39.600 --> 43:42.310
Don't let Miyako catch you

43:39.600 --> 43:42.310
I'm here

43:42.390 --> 43:43.890
<b>Samidare</b>

43:43.890 --> 43:48.360
He was the one who summoned me 
to Miyako's favorite bar that night.

43:50.740 --> 43:52.150
And what do I find...

43:57.320 --> 43:58.810
Aqua did that?

44:00.260 --> 44:03.240
Oh, so that's what it was.

44:05.960 --> 44:07.700
<i>I understand now.</i>

44:08.120 --> 44:10.200
<i>I knew it.</i>

44:11.310 --> 44:14.580
<i>Onii-chan loves me way too much!</i>

44:15.810 --> 44:19.140
<i>He dragged Ichigo-san back 
to the agency for my sake!</i>

44:19.140 --> 44:22.030
<i>His methods are always 
so roundabout and so damn cute!</i>

44:22.430 --> 44:25.600
<i>He was like this even as a doctor.</i>

44:25.600 --> 44:29.060
<i>He'd set up surprises without 
talking to anyone about it.</i>

44:29.510 --> 44:32.950
<i>He's always been nice to a fault. 
No changing it now.</i>

44:32.950 --> 44:35.690
<i>And he still tries to pretend 
to be the bad guy.</i>

44:36.020 --> 44:38.400
<i>But don't worry! 
I get all that about you and more!</i>

44:43.670 --> 44:46.110
Okay, there's just too much 
on her schedule.

44:46.110 --> 44:49.990
But this is Ruby's chance 
to become a household name.

44:49.990 --> 44:52.460
What if work dries up for her later?

44:52.780 --> 44:55.800
Then I'll just go out and get more.

44:58.550 --> 45:00.920
Don't lose sight of the big picture.

45:00.920 --> 45:03.260
Don't be afraid of her 
booming popularity ending.

45:03.260 --> 45:05.970
It's a matter of when, not if.

45:06.610 --> 45:10.230
Relax. Ruby's no flash in the pan.

45:10.660 --> 45:14.110
And it's my job to make sure 
she stays that way.

45:14.830 --> 45:19.020
What we should be doing now 
is making Ruby seem exclusive.

45:19.020 --> 45:22.070
The showrunners need to see her 
as a premium talent.

45:22.510 --> 45:26.380
Give them the runaround and secure 
better-quality gigs for her.

45:26.380 --> 45:31.100
And if possible, focus on 
the gigs that are far in the future.

45:31.100 --> 45:33.700
Don't just accept any work 
that comes her way.

45:33.700 --> 45:36.590
Just being on screen doesn't 
make one a household name.

45:37.030 --> 45:40.730
Only take on shows that are built 
to highlight Ruby's character.

45:40.730 --> 45:42.340
It was the same with Ai, too.

45:42.870 --> 45:45.050
You can turn down all of these.

45:45.430 --> 45:48.270
Also, use her as a bargaining chip 
to barter deals for other talents.

45:48.690 --> 45:51.520
Kana Arima would be 
a big hit on variety shows.

45:51.820 --> 45:54.690
Spread the work 
across everyone in the agency.

45:55.160 --> 45:58.900
Also, you should move to a bigger office.

45:59.810 --> 46:02.850
You gotta make 'em believe 
we're a major joint.

46:04.110 --> 46:05.820
I'm just not good enough.

46:07.560 --> 46:11.810
If you'd run the agency all along, 
it would be so much bigger now.

46:11.810 --> 46:14.040
Nah, you've done amazing.

46:14.470 --> 46:17.810
You built respectful 
working relationships with clients,

46:17.810 --> 46:20.470
brought in work 
without stepping on any toes,

46:20.470 --> 46:22.730
and developed better 
talent in the meantime.

46:23.630 --> 46:28.520
Frankly, Strawberry Pro has a stellar 
reputation within the industry right now.

46:28.520 --> 46:30.560
Never would've happened with me in charge.

46:31.160 --> 46:33.250
It was only possible because of you.

46:43.100 --> 46:46.980
You're not going to win me over 
with obvious sucking up like that.

46:46.980 --> 46:50.580
Once you're done here, you're cleaning 
the sinks and bathrooms.

46:50.920 --> 46:53.290
That wasn't what I was going for, really.

46:55.180 --> 46:58.980
Also, keep a close eye on that kid.

46:58.980 --> 47:00.700
I know.

47:00.700 --> 47:02.510
It's a difficult time for Ruby, but I—

47:02.510 --> 47:03.630
Not her.

47:03.630 --> 47:06.240
It's Aqua we need to keep an eye on.

47:07.930 --> 47:11.020
He's gonna break down soon.

47:11.390 --> 47:14.440
Hell, he might already have.

47:17.690 --> 47:19.270
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

47:20.340 --> 47:23.990
<i>I don't know why, 
but this feels lacking somehow.</i>

47:24.680 --> 47:29.820
<i>Aqua-kun, will this really help you 
complete your revenge?</i>

47:30.950 --> 47:35.690
Filming for <i>The 15-Year Lie</i> 
starts next week.

47:35.690 --> 47:38.170
It's a massive project 
for Strawberry Pro as a whole.

47:38.600 --> 47:41.450
The day after tomorrow, we have the 
full read-through and costume checks.

47:41.450 --> 47:43.890
At dawn in four days, 
we visit the shrine to pray for a hit.

47:43.890 --> 47:45.630
And filming starts in seven days.

47:46.120 --> 47:49.210
We're scheduled to wrap 
in the third week of August.

47:49.210 --> 47:50.970
The last week is reserved as insurance.

47:51.290 --> 47:53.120
I smell a holiday incoming!

47:54.800 --> 47:56.810
But don't you forget.

47:57.260 --> 48:00.250
We have Kana-chan's graduation 
concert at the end of August.

48:00.250 --> 48:03.310
We'll be using the reserved days 
to practice for that.

48:03.310 --> 48:05.610
Uh, about that...

48:05.990 --> 48:09.010
We set up a B-Komachi live tour 
at the end of the year.

48:09.010 --> 48:11.370
That's where Kana Arima 
will be graduating.

48:12.330 --> 48:13.530
The heck?

48:13.530 --> 48:16.580
We were all ready to say goodbye!

48:16.580 --> 48:19.170
We got Arima's okay.

48:19.960 --> 48:24.390
I mean, it's not like 
I <i>have</i> to leave in August.

48:24.390 --> 48:26.580
And we'll all be busy,

48:26.580 --> 48:31.390
so I'd feel bad asking you to make time 
for my graduation concert.

48:31.830 --> 48:35.780
How was I supposed to refuse 
when they insisted?

48:35.780 --> 48:38.720
Here stands the most 
accommodating entertainer of all time.

48:38.720 --> 48:40.760
Pushover doesn't begin to describe her!

48:40.760 --> 48:43.360
Treat yourself better, girl!

48:43.750 --> 48:47.500
Hey, plans never go according to plan.

48:47.500 --> 48:48.820
Hey, Director.

48:48.820 --> 48:50.350
What brings you here today?

48:50.790 --> 48:52.880
Nothing special.

48:53.280 --> 48:55.750
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

48:53.280 --> 48:55.750
<b>Final Version</b>

48:53.590 --> 48:55.750
I just brought the final script.

48:55.750 --> 48:56.960
Whoa!

48:56.960 --> 48:58.560
You brought these personally?

48:58.560 --> 49:00.960
Well, our workplaces are nearby.

49:01.790 --> 49:03.960
And paying for a courier would be a waste.

49:03.960 --> 49:08.420
I don't wanna hear about the financial 
realities of a single man in his 40s.

49:08.860 --> 49:11.660
My name's really on here!

49:11.660 --> 49:13.300
Can I really do this?

49:13.890 --> 49:16.040
Don't worry. You'll do just fine.

49:16.040 --> 49:17.270
Kana-chan!

49:17.270 --> 49:21.460
You've been playing the role of a high 
schooler all these years, after all.

49:21.460 --> 49:23.890
Those are two very different things!

49:24.230 --> 49:29.570
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

49:24.230 --> 49:29.570
<b>Ai (B-Komachi)
Takamiy (B-Komachi)
Nino (B-Komachi)
Mei-Mei (B-Komachi)
Boy A
